==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{af|es|en-|pieza|-ar}}, possibly through a {{inh|es|VL.|-}} root {{m|la|*impettiāre}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{es-IPA}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb|empez|ar|pres=empiezo|pret=empecé}}

# to [[start]], [[begin]], to [[get started]]
#: {{syn|es|comenzar|iniciar}}
#: {{lb|es|with {{l|es|a}}}} to start to
#:: {{ux|es|Hace poco que '''empezó''' a comer vegetales.|He recently '''started''' eating vegetables.}}
#: {{lb|es|with {{l|es|por}}}} to start by; to start with
#:: {{ux|es|Sugiero que '''empecemos''' por reconecer que necesitamos más ayuda.|I suggest that '''we start''' by acknowledging that we need more help.}}
#:: {{ux|es|En español, pocas palabras '''empiezan''' por la letra ñ.|In Spanish, few words '''begin''' with the letter ñ.}}
# {{lb|es|with {{l|es|con}}}} to [[lead]] [[with]], to [[open]] [[with]]

